From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.media.mediacontrol: IInspectable stubs, display properties, controls and events

The FIXME stubs of the DLL, done as Windows behaves:

- GetIids / GetTrustLevel / GetRuntimeClassName of the factory, the
  control, the display updater and the music properties (BaseTrust, the
  interfaces each answers, the WinRT class name); ActivateInstance of the
  factory stays E_NOTIMPL (no default constructor); an unknown IID is
  E_NOINTERFACE without a FIXME; DllGetClassObject has no FIXME.
- SystemMediaTransportControls: SoundLevel (Full: nothing lowers it
  here), the Stop/Record/FastForward/Rewind/ChannelUp/ChannelDown enabled
  properties (FALSE by default, round-tripping), ButtonPressed and
  PropertyChanged registrations (unique tokens, the handler referenced
  until removed; removing an unknown token is S_OK; never raised, there
  is no system media UI). DisplayUpdater is one object per control.
- DisplayUpdater: AppMediaId, Thumbnail (referenced), MusicProperties
  (one object for the updater's life), ClearAll (every value cleared,
  Type back to Unknown), Update.
- MusicDisplayProperties: AlbumArtist, TrackNumber and Genres, the
  latter a real IVector<HSTRING> (vector.c) with its view and iterator:
  E_BOUNDS for bad indexes, E_CHANGED_STATE for an iterator whose list
  changed. The properties object no longer leaks AlbumTitle.
- GetForWindow no longer logs an uninitialised pointer or leaks the
  control on an unsupported IID.

Left as they were (see the note): the 8 AudioStateMonitor spec stubs,
VideoProperties, ImageProperties and CopyFromFileAsync.

